# Bridged admin dashboard

This file used to describe an Ant Design + custom CSS stack. That stack was removed in the v3 revamp.
The single source of truth for every coding agent is now:

- `AGENTS.md`: commands, stack, non-negotiables, git rules, definition of done
- `docs/design-system.md`: the UI standard, shared with the Bridged portal (mandatory for any visible change)
- `docs/architecture.md`: routing, folder convention, data layer, theme
- `docs/product-rules.md`: admin rules (team owner first, Claude OAuth flow, URL tokens, custom work status)

Read them before making changes. In short:

- React 19, JSX, Tailwind CSS 4 and shadcn/ui (`src/components/ui`), plus the Bridged app components in `src/components` and Hugeicons. No antd, no new CSS files, no hex colours.
- Use brand tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`). Every change must work in light and dark mode and on phones.
- Copy is UK English and sentence case. Dates are day first via `formatDate`. Success toasts are past tense; error toasts read "Couldn't …".
- Follow the folder convention: `pages/` → `presentation/<feature>/{workflows,components,controllers,skeletons}`. All endpoints go in `services/api.js`, and RTK Query triggers are named `_FETCH_X`.
- In UI tasks, change only the UI. Never push to `main` or `staging`.
